/*

In this kata you will have to write a function that takes litres and price_per_litre (in dollar) as arguments.

Purchases of 2 or more litres get a discount of 5 cents per litre, purchases of 4 or more litres get a discount of 10 cents per litre, and so on every two litres, up to a maximum discount of 25 cents per litre. But total discount per litre cannot be more than 25 cents. Return the total cost rounded to 2 decimal places. Also you can guess that there will not be negative or non-numeric inputs.

Good Luck!

Note

1 Dollar = 100 Cents



*/



def fuel_price(litres, price_per_litre):
    a = 0.05 
    b = 0.10 
    c = 0.15 
    d = 0.2 
    e = 0.25
    if (litres >= 2 and litres < 4):
        return round((litres * price_per_litre - litres * a) * 100 ,2)/ 100
    elif (litres >= 4 and litres < 6):
        return round((litres * price_per_litre - litres * b) * 100,2) / 100
    elif (litres >= 6 and litres < 8):
        return round((litres * price_per_litre - litres * c) * 100,2) / 100
    elif (litres >= 8 and litres < 10):
        return round((litres * price_per_litre - litres * d) * 100,2) / 100
    else:
        return round((litres * price_per_litre - litres * e) * 100,2) / 100
